  "body": "While implementing COOP, I ran into \"enforce a response's opener policy\" not passing \"check if COOP values require a browsing context group switch\" in an order that matches its declaration. Reviewing that fix with AI turned up a few more issues nearby, which this fixes too.\n\nChanges:\n\n- fix COOP group switch check argument order\n- fix undefined variable in report-only COOP check\n- fix type confusion in popup COOP check\n- fix link to access to another window COOP report\n- fix COOP access from an opened window report body\n\n\nReporting integration seems to have some further problems (e.g github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8336, github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11365), but I've tried keeping this bit smaller.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13026/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 3, 2026, 9:16 AM UTC (77e3ad3)\">/browsers.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13026/0cd3220...77e3ad3/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 3, 2026, 9:16 AM UTC (77e3ad3)\">diff</a> )",
